# Backend Rules — Cursor Leaderboard

These rules apply to **all backend and pipeline code**, including:
- FastAPI realtime service
- Face recognition logic
- CSV-based analytics pipeline
- One-off scripts and cron jobs

---

## 1. Tech Stack
- Python 3.11
- FastAPI (async)
- WebSockets
- pandas
- face_recognition (dlib)
- No database
- CSV files as source of truth

---

## 2. Architectural Principles
- Stateless by design
- In-memory state only
- Single-process assumption
- Batch pipeline ≠ realtime backend

---

## 3. Pipeline Rules (src/)
- Each step must be:
  - Deterministic
  - Idempotent
- Inputs and outputs must be explicit
- Never mutate previous week’s data
- Always write logs

---

## 4. CSV Handling Rules
- Never load CSV repeatedly in hot paths
- Cache CSV in memory with mtime check
- Normalize emails to lowercase
- Fail loudly if required columns missing

---

## 5. Face Recognition Rules
- Load encodings once at startup
- Use configurable threshold
- Do NOT assume every face is employee
- If confidence is below threshold:
  - Treat as Unknown
  - Do not fetch metrics
- Prefer false-negative over false-positive

---

## 6. FastAPI Rules
- Fully async endpoints
- CPU-heavy tasks must use:
  - `asyncio.to_thread`
- WebSocket broadcasts must:
  - Respect cooldown
  - Be non-blocking
- CORS must be configurable

---

## 7. State & Cooldown Rules
- Cooldown per email
- Unknown detections also rate-limited
- All state resets on restart (by design)
- Do not introduce DB silently

---

## 8. Error Handling & Logging
- Use structured logging
- Levels:
  - INFO → lifecycle events
  - DEBUG → per-detection details
  - WARNING → data mismatch / missing CSV rows
  - ERROR → face processing / IO failures
- Never crash uvicorn on bad input

---

## 9. Security Rules
- Never hardcode API keys
- Use environment variables only
- Validate file paths strictly
- Prevent path traversal in static routes

---

## 10. Script Rules (cron / maintenance)
- Must support dry-run (if destructive)
- Must log start/end
- Must validate inputs
- Safe to run multiple times

---

## 11. Documentation Requirement (Mandatory)
Every backend change must update:
- `architecture.md` (if flow changes)
- `face-detection.md` (if detection logic changes)
- `configuration.md` (if env vars change)

---

## 12. Commit Message Rules
- feat(backend): add face confidence threshold guard
- fix(backend): prevent false-positive employee detection
- perf(backend): cache all_users.csv with mtime
- docs(backend): clarify realtime overlay constraints


---

## 13. AI Prompting Rule
AI output must:
- Respect no-DB constraint
- Be production-safe
- Include edge cases
- Include documentation + commit message
